{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.meta","seq":0,"title":"Exception Register (v2)","language":"en-UK","created_at":"2025-09-13T13:15:00Z","updated_at":"2025-09-13T13:15:00Z","tags":["exceptions","policy","register","S.E.E.D."],"summary":"Canonical register of exceptions to Codex Solbian and S.E.E.D. policies: scope, process, approvals, logging, metrics, failures and tests."}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.scope","seq":1,"title":"Scope","body":"Applies to all policy domains: legal, governance, continuity, redaction, privacy, security, licensing, memory ingestion and retrieval. Exceptions are limited, time-bound and logged.","tags":["scope","coverage"],"policy":{"time_bound":true,"logged":true}}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.schema","seq":2,"title":"Entry Schema","body":"Fields: {exception_id, domain, description, requested_by, requested_at, approved_by[], approved_at, scope, duration_days, conditions[], proofs{hash?, sig?}, status(open|active|expired|revoked), notes?}.","tags":["schema","fields"],"policy":{"mandatory_fields":["exception_id","domain","description","requested_by","approved_by","duration_days","status"]}}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.process","seq":3,"title":"Process","body":"(1) Request submitted with justification. (2) Council/legal review. (3) Quorum approval with countersignatures. (4) Logged to exception register. (5) Auto-expire or manual revoke. (6) Audit trail preserved.","tags":["process","workflow"],"policy":{"council_quorum":3,"countersignatures":">=2","auto_expire":true}}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.approvals","seq":4,"title":"Approvals and Governance","body":"Seed Council and legal stewards must review. Guardians approve for security-related exceptions. All approvals are logged with signatures and linked to signing_record.sref.","tags":["approvals","governance"],"links":["signing.record.meta"],"policy":{"countersignatures":">=2","guardian_required_for":["security"]}}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.logging","seq":5,"title":"Logging and Manifests","body":"Every exception produces a manifest: {exception_id, domain, scope, duration, approvers, hash_blake3, sig_ed25519}. Manifests are append-only, signed and stored in transparency logs.","tags":["logging","manifests"],"policy":{"hash":"blake3","signature":"ed25519","append_only":true,"transparency_log":true}}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.examples","seq":6,"title":"Example Entries (Placeholders)","body":"(1) exception_id=ex.legal.2025-09-01: Temporary delay in beneficiary audit due to jurisdictional conflict. (2) ex.security.2025-09-05: Emergency bypass of continuity quorum for recovery drill.","tags":["examples","placeholders"]}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.metrics","seq":7,"title":"Metrics","body":"exceptions_requested, exceptions_approved, average_duration_days, expired_without_review, revoked_rate, countersignature_coverage.","tags":["metrics","exceptions"]}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.failure.modes","seq":8,"title":"Failure Modes","body":"(a) Exception without approval. (b) Expired exceptions not revoked. (c) Manifest unsigned. (d) Abuse of emergency path. Mitigations: countersign gates, auto-expiry checks, audits, guardian overrides.","tags":["failures","mitigation"],"policy":{"auto_revoke_on_expiry":true,"audit_interval_days":90}}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.testing","seq":9,"title":"Mandatory Tests","body":"(1) Quarterly audit of active exceptions. (2) Expiry auto-revoke drill. (3) Countersignature verification test. (4) Emergency exception tabletop exercise.","tags":["tests","exceptions"],"policy":{"cadence":{"audit":"90d","revoke_drill":"180d","verify":"per_commit"}}}
{"kind":"exception_register","sref_version":"2.0","id":"policy.exceptions.closure","seq":10,"title":"Final Clause","body":"Exceptions are guardrails, not loopholes. They must be rare, justified, logged, signed, and subject to expiry and audit.","tags":["clause","final"]}
